# =============================================================================
# CODEOWNERS - review ownership
#
# NEVER INHERITED. GitHub reads this only from the repository that owns it, so
# unlike the community health files it cannot come from the account's .github
# repository and has to live here.
#
# ONE OWNER, SO ONE RULE. This template is private and single-maintainer, so
# the owner is known at authoring time rather than guessed at. That is the
# difference from the public template, which ships every rule commented out
# because it cannot know who will generate from it - and a rule naming an
# owner without write access is a GitHub error, not a warning.
#
# Additional path rules would all name the same person, which adds lines
# without adding information. Add them when a second maintainer exists, or when
# a specific directory should route somewhere else.
#
# ⚠️ THIS DOES NOT BLOCK YOUR OWN PULL REQUESTS. The shipped rulesets require
# zero approvals and do not require code-owner review, so a solo maintainer
# cannot deadlock on being unable to approve their own work. What this does
# give you is an automatic review request on anything opened by somebody else -
# Dependabot, or an agent acting on your behalf.
#
# PRECEDENCE: the LAST matching rule wins. Broad defaults first, specific
# overrides below.
# =============================================================================

# Everything, unless a later rule says otherwise.
